A||N||7||Bluebottlejunky||How to know if your clutch pedal is bent?||||1||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||04-14-2001||09:59 PM||||My clutch pedal I think is bent..It is about an inch below the brake.  Is it true that is should be about an inch above the brake?  If so I think I will be needing a new steel one from the fiero store. Thanks alot..I bet u gys are getting sick of all the clutch stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I wish my spell check would work on my computer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>BBJ<BR>85' GT 4sp||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||04-14-2001||10:11 PM||||The clutch pedal should be about 1 inch above the brake pedal.  <P>You can probably just bend the original pedal back either in the car or out.  Might be worth a try before you go out and buy the new pedal and linkage rod (If you have an 84-85).  <P>When I put the steel pedal on my 85 it did not rest as high as I wanted it to comapred to the brake.  I removed it and mounted it in a vice and carefully bent the bracket into I got it where I wanted it.  Improved the pedal action greatly.<P>Good luck...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||04-14-2001||10:14 PM||||I just saw that the Fierostore dose sell them for like 30 bucks.  how hard is it to put a new one in? Time/1-10?  So dose it make it harder that I have an 85 4sp?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-14-2001||11:17 PM||||It goes quick!<BR>Scale of 1-10?<BR>Less than an hour for the novice, 10 minutes or so for those who know how it goes together.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bluebottlejunky||04-14-2001||11:26 PM||||Hmmmmmm, I think i will have to invest in a new one! hehe  Thanks alot guys.  Is there other places that I can get one other than Fiero Store?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
