Z||000006||NSUMEY||04-16-2001||09:54 AM||||your local Pontiac dealer should be able to get you a new one...just got one for 32bucks.....is your old one aluminium? if it is..change it   <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>   for referance ||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||04-16-2001||02:06 PM||||If I remember correctly, you can tell if its bent by taking it out. Where the pedal pivoted, put a penci through and look directly down. The pencil should be completely parellal with the arm that actually pushes the master cyl rod. If it ain't, it ain't straight. I would say to take it out first and see. Bending it back might be a temp solution but I would imagine that the metal would have "memory" and be more apt to bend back where it was.<P>Pedal height has always associated (in my experience) with how the hydraulics are doing. <P>Unless its really bent badly! :0||||reg||14
